Method and Terminology Attribution

The Damped Resonance Alignment method (Phase III/IV) and the native multi-axis Manifold extension (Phase V), the Pusula runtime-construction technique, and the complete original terminology defined in this repository are original contributions first published here by Akbas -- June 2026 (DRA, v1.2) and September 2026 (Manifold extension, v2.0-DRA). These are documented with full mathematical specification, a public timestamped commit history, a set of permanent Zenodo DOIs (listed below), and a parallel public test-log record on r/TinyLlama_TITAN and r/TinyLlama_AGI, which together constitute the canonical reference for this method and terminology.

Suggested citation:

Akbas. AkbasCore: Damped Resonance Alignment and the Native Multi-Axis
Manifold Extension -- A Sub-Threshold Inference-Layer Steering Framework
for Transformer Models. GitHub repository, v2.0-DRA, September 2026.
https://github.com/ceceli33/titan-cognitive-core
DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.22715555

Permanent, version-pinned archival records on Zenodo:

v1.2 -- AkbasCore 1.2 -- Damped Resonance Alignment -- DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21356271
v1.2.0 -- AkbasCore 1.2 -- Damped Resonance Alignment -- DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22396352
v2.0-DRA -- AkbasCore 2.0 -- DRA/MANIFOLD -- DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22715555

